        <body>
            <div xml:id="d398">

                <pb facs="0404" n="398" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg398"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">012.3/7849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Algiers (Cole) to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1942-10-18T20:30:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1942-10-17T00:00:00-05:00">undated</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        October 18, 1942—8:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>691. For Admiral Leahy from Murphy. You might be interested in knowing that
                    Darlan’s son, Alain, has just entered an Algiers hospital and according to
                    present diagnosis he is suffering from infantile paralysis.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tuck. [Murphy.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cole</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
